Got it — I read the image and your explanation. What you’re really asking for is a **clean, enterprise-ready Confluence document structure + labels** that formalize the **GenAI experimentation → production → MLOps handoff flow**.

Below is a **Confluence-ready document** you can paste almost as-is, plus **labels** to make it discoverable.

---

## 📄 Confluence Page Title

**GenAI Use Case Intake, Experimentation, and Production Governance Framework**

---

## 🧭 Purpose

This document defines the **standardized lifecycle, approvals, documentation, and ownership model** for all GenAI use cases entering the **GenAI Experimentation Platform**, progressing to **Production**, and transitioning to **MLOps ownership**.

---

## 🧱 Scope

Applies to **all GenAI / LLM-based use cases**, including but not limited to:

* Comms (In Production)
* Client Summary (Architecture Review Pending)
* LLM Blueprint (Managed Responsibility Model)
* Dicer / Datadog

---

## 🔁 GenAI Use Case Lifecycle Overview

### 1️⃣ Use Case Intake → Experimentation

All incoming use cases must start in **GenAI Experimentation**.

**Mandatory artifacts before experimentation:**

* ✅ **MRGR Approval**
* ✅ **PRD (Experimentation Scope)**
* ✅ **LUMA – Experimentation**
* ✅ **DUC – Experimentation**

> Purpose: Validate feasibility, value, and risk before production intent.

---

### 2️⃣ Experimentation Completion Gate

Once experimentation is completed, the use case owner must explicitly declare:

> “Experimentation is complete. Requesting approval to proceed with **GenAI Production Serving**.”

---

### 3️⃣ Production Serving Enablement

For GenAI / LLM-based production applications, **new governance artifacts are required**, independent of experimentation approvals.

**Mandatory artifacts for Production Serving:**

* ✅ **PRD (Production Scope)**

  * Includes **Mosaic ID**
* ✅ **LUMA – Serving**
* ✅ **DUC – Serving**
* ✅ **Architecture Review Approval**
* ✅ **Security & Compliance Review**

> Note: Experimentation LUMA/DUC **cannot** be reused for Serving.

---

### 4️⃣ Production Deployment

After approvals:

* Application is deployed to **Production**
* Ownership transitions to **MLOps**

---

### 5️⃣ MLOps Ownership & Maintenance

Once in production, **ongoing responsibility moves to MLOps**.

**MLOps Team:**

* Milan
* Anurag

**MLOps Responsibilities:**

* Model/application monitoring
* Reliability & uptime
* Performance optimization
* Incident response
* Continuous improvement

---

## 🧩 Use Case Status Examples

### ✅ Comms

* Status: **In Production**
* Phase: MLOps Ownership

### ⏳ Client Summary

* Status: **Architecture Review Pending**
* Phase: Experimentation → Production Gate

### 🧠 LLM Blueprint

* Status: **Managed Responsibility Model**
* Phase: Platform / Blueprint Enablement

### 📊 Dicer / Datadog

* Status: **Production-bound**
* Phase: PRD + Serving Governance

---

## 🛡 Governance Principles

* No GenAI use case goes to production without:

  * MRGR approval
  * PRD (with Mosaic ID)
  * Serving-specific LUMA & DUC
* Experimentation ≠ Production
* MLOps ownership begins **only after production cutover**

---

